        "reported_material_gaps": [],
        "research_rationale": "EO 10843 creates the Taft-Hartley Board of Inquiry for the 1959 steel dispute; provisional status no. I read the held registered Federal Register text, confirmed identity, and confirmed a single-clause inventory. The report date was amended by EO 10848 (a later event with before and after text). The own-terms contingent end (termination by the President) is not shown by any held evidence and is disclosed. EO 12553 (1986-02-25) revokes the order and its amendment and is the first end in held evidence.\nMember checks: {\"earlier_end_check\":\"Searched for an end earlier than 1986-02-25. EO 10848 amends the report date and is a later event, not an end. The own-terms contingent end is termination of the board by the President; no held text shows one (a Cruden regular-expression search of held order texts for a board of inquiry being terminated found no match), and this absence is disclosed. The dossier lists no conflict and no missing item. An unnamed instrument would not end the order (owner ruling 2026-10-21 unnamed instruments).\",\"independent_command_check\":\"No independent command survives: creation of the board was performed on issue; the report deadline passed; the clause keeping the board in existence until presidential termination ended with the order on revocation. The order creates no delegation or rule that outlived the board.\",\"savings_check\":\"No saving language in EO 12553 (held text searched); nothing in the order depends on a separate surviving authority.\",\"scope_check\":\"The whole order is covered by EO 12553, which lists EO 10843 and its amendment EO 10848 and revokes listed orders and amendments without exception. Inventory is a single clause; the held text shows creation, report deadline and continued existence as its only commands.\"}",
